<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 12.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 12.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Vitorandis	40,883   Feb 27    Mar 14     Dongkuk</p>
<p> Comos Trader    33,219   Mar 7     Mar 16     Inchon</p>
<p> Baltic Trident  52,000   Mar 18    Mar 30     Inchon</p>
<p> Jade Orient     26,000   Mar 26		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Cargo	     39,311   Mar 17	-	  Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Trans Bridge    29,502   Mar 5     Mar 19     Kisco</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Joy Venture     38,500   Feb 28    Mar 17     Kangwon</p>
<p> Pack Duke	 25,000   Mar 7     Mar 22     POSCO</p>
<p> Fruition	  30,000   Mar 9     Mar 24     POSCO</p>
<p> Xing Su Hai     22,000   End-Mar		  Kangwon</p>
<p> T.B.N	     30,000   Mid-Apr		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule as yet</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Sea Glory	 27,703   Mar 17		   Hanbo</p>
<p> Kalma	     31,263   Mar 18		   Hanbo</p>
<p> Rainbow Sky     10,000   Mar 26		   Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
